<title>BRAZIL: SOCCER-BRAZILIAN SOCCER RESULTS/STANDINGS.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-BRAZILIAN SOCCER RESULTS/STANDINGS.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1997-05-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results of Brazilian</p>
<p>soccer matches played at the weekend.</p>
<p>Sao Paulo championship</p>
<p> America-S.J.Rio Preto   3    Rio Branco		   2</p>
<p> Botafogo-Ribeirao Preto 3    Aracatuba		    2</p>
<p> Guarani		     1    Portuguesa Santista	0</p>
<p> Juventus		    3    Mogi Mirim		   1</p>
<p> Palmeiras		   1    Uniao Sao Joao	     3</p>
<p> Portuguesa		  1    Internacional Limeira    1</p>
<p> Santos			2    Corinthians		  0</p>
<p> Sao Jose		    1    Sao Paulo		    1</p>
<p>Group One</p>
<p> Palmeiras		 21 12  6  3 52 27 42</p>
<p> Portuguesa		21 11  7  3 43 27 40</p>
<p> Santos		    21 11  7  3 39 23 40</p>
<p> Guarani		   21  6  8  7 35 44 26</p>
<p> Sao Jose		  21  4  8  9 26 36 20</p>
<p> Juventus		  21  4  6 11 36 51 18</p>
<p> Botafogo		  21  3  8 10 17 29 17</p>
<p> America		   21  4  4 13 24 57 16</p>
<p>Group two</p>
<p> Corinthians	     21 12  5  4 47 25 41</p>
<p> Sao Paulo		 21  9 10  2 45 23 37</p>
<p> Uniao Sao Joao	  21  8  6  7 31 28 30</p>
<p> Rio Branco		21  7  6  8 29 31 27</p>
<p> Aracatuba		 21  7  5  9 27 29 26</p>
<p>Internacional Limeira 21  6  8  7 34 35 26</p>
<p> Portuguesa Santista   21  6  5 10 26 37 23</p>
<p> Mogi Mirim		21  5  7  9 26 35 22</p>
<p>Note: The teams play once against the other teams in</p>
<p>their own group, then twice against the teams in the other</p>
<p>group. At the end of this, the top two teams in each group</p>
<p>qualify for the final play-off stage. If teams are level on</p>
<p>points, positions are decided by the number of games won.</p>
<p>Corinthians and Sao Paulo already qualified.</p>
<p>Rio de Janeiro championship, third stage</p>
<p> Flamengo		    1    Botafogo		     1</p>
<p> Fluminense		  2    Bangu			  1</p>
<p>Standings</p>
<p> Fluminense		   1  1  0  0  2  1  3</p>
<p> Americano		    1  0  1  0  1  1  1</p>
<p> Botafogo		     1  0  1  0  1  1  1</p>
<p> Flamengo		     1  0  1  0  1  1  1</p>
<p> Vasco da Gama		1  0  1  0  1  1  1</p>
<p> Bangu			  1  0  0  1  1  2  0</p>
<p>Note: the winners of the first, second and third stages</p>
<p>qualify for the final round. Only the top eight in the first</p>
<p>stage go into the second stage and the top six teams in the</p>
<p>second stage carry on into the third stage. If the same team</p>
<p>wins all three stages, they become champions automatically.</p>
<p>    First stage winners - Botafogo   </p>
<p>Second stage winners - Botafogo</p>
<p>Eliminated in the first stage - Itaperuna, America,</p>
<p>Olaria, Barreira.</p>
<p>Eliminated in the second stage - Madureira, Volta Redonda</p>
